Bugfix: Compute the file cache path hash correctly on Oracle

Oracle cannot store empty strings, so the file cache converts them to null
before writing a row. For the storage root, whose path is the empty string,
that left md5() being called with null: on PHP 8 that raises a deprecation
notice, and the resulting path_hash was the hash of null rather than the hash
of the empty string used on every other database.

The value is now cast back to a string before hashing, so path_hash for the
storage root is md5('') on Oracle as well.

https://github.com/owncloud/core/pull/41808
